# Frontend architecture

Organize by **feature**, not by component type.

```
frontend/src/
  app/          # shell: App.tsx, api, realtime, theme shared.tsx, ui kit
  shared/       # cross-feature utilities (routing, countryIso, perf, …)
  features/     # domain features (messages, admin, auth, landing, …)
```

## Rules

- Put new domain UI under `features/<name>/`. Keep `app/` for shell and cross-cutting I/O.
- Prefer extracting **hooks / services / helpers / types** from large pages over many tiny presentational wrappers.
- Ideal file size ~200–600 lines; major pages may be 600–900. Revisit carefully above ~1000.
- Reuse `@/app/api` and `@/app/realtime` — no scattered raw `fetch` / extra Socket.IO clients.
- One Socket.IO connection per session (`realtime.ts`); features subscribe via helpers/hooks.
- Do not invent a global store for state used by a single feature.
- Each major feature should keep a short `README.md` with purpose and entry points.

## Naming

- Components: PascalCase · Hooks: `useSomething` · Utils: camelCase · Constants: UPPER_SNAKE when appropriate · Types: PascalCase
